  "conclusions": [
    "Every custody Worker invocation and every wallet object ran in one location, HKG. Distance does not explain the dispatch cost.",
    "A Worker reaches a wallet object in 14-23 ms when its server already called that object, and in 308-872 ms otherwise.",
    "From another server, the first call to an object addressed by unique ID took 9-18 ms. The first call to an object addressed by name took 419-513 ms unless that server had called it before.",
    "Creating an object took 599-979 ms by unique ID and 667-674 ms by name.",
    "Some Worker invocations started 99-303 ms after their event, with matching CPU. That is isolate start for 9-16 MB modules.",
    "The Gateway is co-located with its database. Deriver A, Deriver B and Signing Worker databases sit in three other locations."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Three wallets per run. The counts show the pattern; they do not establish rates.",
    "The trace request reports the Cloudflare location and server that served it, taken as the location of the caller.",
    "Probe objects held no storage. A wallet object with storage may add work to a first call.",
    "The dispatch probe ran in the Router wallet namespace only.",
    "Application clocks advance only at I/O."
  ],
  "restoration": {
    "allThirteenOriginalVersionsRestoredAfterEachRun": true,
    "observersStopped": true,
    "newResources": 0
  },
